# Strict cross-origin isolation on EVERY response of the docs site (house rule).
# `_headers` is honored by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. CI retains the bundle as a private
# artifact rather than deploying it. A static host that ignores this file must configure the
# same headers itself. Runnable guests still execute in opaque-origin sandbox frames with
# grant-derived CSP; these response headers add document/process isolation around the trusted
# page and must not be presented as active on a host that did not install them.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
